WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.810
A new Game of Thrones preview is out, and
it reveals some big stuff about Season 7 – so

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.810
let’s have a look.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.519
We see more of this sea battle when Euron
Greyjoy attacks Dany’s fleet.

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:14.940
Theon and Yara are there, and Tyene, and Ellaria.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.510
And it looks things go badly for them.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:22.790
Cause later, Euron rolls into King’s Landing
and gives Cersei his gift.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:28.160
And the gift appears to be – Ellaria and
Tyene and what looks like Yara.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.100
It’s hard to be sure with this shot, but
Cersei does at least appear to have some of

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.690
the Sand Snakes – which is probably going
to get ugly.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.890
Cause remember, Ellaria used poison to murder
Cersei’s daughter Myrcella.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:45.460
This is Cersei’s chance to get revenge.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:51.100
We also see Cersei make an alliance with Randyll
Tarly and the recast Dickon Tarly – Sam’s

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.100
family.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.280
The Tarlys are bannermen of the Tyrells, who
are supporting Daenerys – but it looks like

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.500
Randyll changes sides to support Cersei.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.890
Which could be a big deal – House Tarly
has a powerful military, and will make the

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.719
Lannisters even stronger.

00:01:05.719 --> 00:01:10.630
We see Jaime leading Lannisters at this castle,
which judging from all the greenery might

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.320
be Highgarden, seat of the Tyrells.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.670
If the Lannisters take out Highgarden and
capture Sand Snakes in the next couple episodes,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.389
that’d be a strong start for Queen Cersei
this season.

00:01:21.389 --> 00:01:26.560
But things might not go so well for her in
this battle, at what might be Casterly Rock.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.399
Dany’s Unsullied might just take the Lannister
home base.

00:01:30.399 --> 00:01:38.119
Up north, Littlefinger gets all metaphysical,
saying that all possible universes exist simultaneously

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:39.759
or something.

00:01:39.759 --> 00:01:42.420
This guy’s getting more incoherent by the
episode.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.990
His plan now seems to be to divide and undermine
the north.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.389
But is that even in his interests?

00:01:48.389 --> 00:01:50.999
He does know the white walkers are real, right?

00:01:50.999 --> 00:01:55.450
How’s his “chaos is a ladder” gonna
help him when a zombie giant’s running him

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:56.450
down?

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.469
The plotters and the schemers take a back
seat this season – the show’s now more

00:02:00.469 --> 00:02:03.579
about the simple fight to survive.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:08.320
While Petyr speaks in abstractions, the Starks
get pragmatic, and prepare Winterfell for

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.409
the war to come.

00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:13.769
They’re training children to fight, and
generally speaking, when someone conscripts

00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:18.860
child soldiers to fight zombies – they’re
usually considered a bad guy.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.780
But our hero Jon Snow’s the Joe Kony of
this show.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.739
Game of Thrones isn’t about good versus
evil – it’s more a lesser evil versus

00:02:27.739 --> 00:02:33.920
a greater evil versus a super duper ultra
evil versus whatever Littlefinger’s trying

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.989
to be.

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:39.550
Anyway Jon Snow considers an alliance with
Daenerys – cause her dragons might be their

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.540
best hope of beating the army of the dead.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.720
Also Dragonstone has the obsidian that they
need to kill white walkers.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.530
Daenerys gets a visit from Melisandre.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.510
Which could be important, cause Dany came
to Dragonstone with the goal of taking the

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:54.510
Throne.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:59.329
Melisandre can tell her of the more important
war – the war for the dawn against the white

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:00.450
walkers.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:05.099
Mel says Dany has “a role to play … as
does another”.

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:10.540
It sounds like Mel is talking about Azor Ahai,
a hero prophesied to save the world.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.770
In the books, there are complex hints and
connections which suggest one character or

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.890
another might be this saviour.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:22.050
Mel seems to be hinting at what a lot of fans
believe – that Jon Snow and Daenerys are

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.510
both Azor Ahai.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:29.150
Ice and fire, combined – to save the world
from the long night.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.239
Thanks for watching.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:35.159
Quick heads up – there’s a channel called
Alt Schwift X posting Game of Thrones videos

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:41.409
in like the style of Alt Shift X – except
they’re wildly inaccurate, and frankly unprofessional

00:03:41.409 --> 00:03:45.799
– so make sure you avoid that channel and
do not watch this video under any circumstances.

